# CRUD Web Application using Flask

A simple CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) web application built using Python Flask, HTML, and CSS. This project allows users to add, view, edit, update, and delete records through a clean and user-friendly web interface.

## Features

- Create new records with Name and Age
- View all records in a table
- Edit existing records
- Update record details
- Delete records
- Simple and responsive UI
- Beginner-friendly Flask project

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Flask
- HTML5
- CSS3

## Project Structure

```text
CRUD/
│
├── app.py
│
├── templates/
│   └── index.html
│
└── static/
    └── style.css
```

## Installation

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/crud-flask-app.git
cd crud-flask-app
```

### 2. Install Flask

```bash
pip install flask
```

### 3. Run the Application

```bash
python app.py
```

### 4. Open in Browser

```text
http://127.0.0.1:5000
```

## How It Works

1. Enter a Name and Age.
2. Click the **Add** button to create a new record.
3. Records are displayed in a table.
4. Use the **Edit** button to modify a record.
5. Click **Update** to save changes.
6. Use the **Delete** button to remove a record.

## Learning Outcomes

This project helped in understanding:

- Flask routing
- Form handling in Flask
- Dynamic HTML rendering using Jinja2
- CRUD operations
- Frontend design with HTML and CSS
- Basic web application development

